{"id": "EUVD-2026-7675", "enisaUuid": "7a0887c6-8d18-3d3d-807c-8b5ba33254fd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: add chann_lock to protect ksmbd_chann_list xarray\n\nksmbd_chann_list xarray lacks synchronization, allowing use-after-free in\nmulti-channel sessions (between lookup_chann_list() and ksmbd_chann_del).\n\nAdds rw_semaphore chann_lock to struct ksmbd_session and protects\nall xa_load/xa_store/xa_erase accesses.", "datePublished": "2026-02-18T14:53:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:39:01", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/43ad494ac6e940a8eabf25d5bd77bb3bb53b1153", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4c2ca31608521895dd742a43beca4b4d29762345", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e4a8a96a93d08570e0405cfd989a8a07e5b6ff33", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/36ef605c0395b94b826a8c8d6f2697071173de6e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4f3a06cc57976cafa8c6f716646be6c79a99e485"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-23226", "GHSA-5jgq-pv8m-5cx7"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.48, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "035831ca-ebb1-3602-8f7d-66f6237d76c9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d9c4172110e645b383ff13eee759728d74f1a5d <4f3a06cc57976cafa8c6f716646be6c79a99e485"}, {"id": "0523690b-6245-3166-b943-8dea10cb9efc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19.1"}, {"id": "09a65b36-4a99-323d-8adf-99a037aeb089", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "0e3d2169-8293-388d-994e-1eba621e92cb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.2.16 <6.3"}, {"id": "11529533-5c59-3eb1-9c9f-e99cc56700d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b1caecbf34b8c8260d851ec4efde71f3694460b7"}, {"id": "13